        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Syndicalism</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1895 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Thinkers</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-joseph-proudhon">Pierre-Joseph Proudhon</a>, whose mutualism was its direct root; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-bakunin">Mikhail Bakunin</a>, who advocated the general strike; Émile Pouget, anarchist and CGT leader who backed sabotage and direct action; Victor Griffuelhes of the CGT; Bill Haywood and Vincent St. John of the IWW; James Larkin of the Irish ITGWU; Tom Mann of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>; Rudolf Rocker, who wrote the FAUD's programme; Georges Sorel, whose Reflections on Violence brought syndicalist ideas to a wider audience</span></div>
